---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';
const base='/equipment/12-03/', brochure='https://asset-downloads.zeiss.com/catalogs/download/mic/05fd8acd-c539-4a72-979d-c454c578e3d8/EN_product-info_LSM-980.pdf', manual='https://www.zeiss.com.sg/content/dam/rms/countries/singapore/apac/lsm980-manual.pdf';
---
<Layout pageTitle="ZEISS LSM 980 · passive synthetic planes" description="Inspect a stationary ZEISS side-port layout and view XY, XZ, and YZ sections of an analytic inert intensity phantom." wide={true}>
<article class="equipment lsm"><nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/12-03/">← Equipment 12-03</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Equipment register</a><a href="#lsm-evidence">References and verification</a></nav>
<header class="eq-mast"><span class="eq-meta">12-03 · DOCUMENTARY MODEL & SYNTHETIC STACK / FIRST PASS</span><h2>ZEISS LSM 980 with Airyscan 2</h2><p>Orbit the inactive microscope assembly and compare the widths of one artificial intensity spot in three orthogonal planes. Try the constant-background track to see why it has no measurable width.</p></header>
<div class="grid"><section><h3>Stationary side-port system</h3><div id="lsm-view" aria-label="Orbitable documentary Axio Observer stand, side-port scan head, detector housing and separate generic display"></div>
<div class="bar"><button data-lsm-view="overall">Reset view</button><button data-lsm-view="optics">Stand and scan head</button><button data-lsm-view="display">Teaching display</button><button id="lsm-cycle">Next display plane</button></div>
<p id="lsm-ready" role="status">Loading metric model…</p><p>The microscope is inactive. Drag to orbit and pinch or scroll to zoom. The teal pad on the generic workstation rotates through the displayed planes, not hardware states.</p></section>
<section><h3>Analytic intensity phantom</h3><canvas id="lsm-plot" width="700" height="435" aria-label="Synthetic inert spot with an object-space scale bar"></canvas>
<div class="fields"><label>Display plane<select id="lsm-orientation"><option value="XY">XY</option><option value="XZ">XZ</option><option value="YZ">YZ</option></select></label><label>Display track<select id="lsm-channel"><option value="signal">Synthetic raised spot</option><option value="background">Constant background</option></select></label><label>Plane index<input id="lsm-slice" type="range" min="0" max="30" step="1" value="15"/></label></div>
<div class="bar"><button class="primary" id="lsm-measure">Measure phantom widths</button><button id="lsm-reset">Reset</button></div><p id="lsm-status" aria-live="polite">Select a plane, then measure the three center-line widths.</p><output id="lsm-result"></output><div class="bar"><button id="lsm-png" disabled>Plane PNG</button><button id="lsm-csv" disabled>Plane CSV</button><button id="lsm-json" disabled>Inspection JSON</button></div></section></div>
<section id="lsm-evidence"><h3>Geometry and evidence</h3><p>Selected configuration: ZEISS LSM 980 side-port with Airyscan 2 on an inverted Axio Observer-type stand. <a href={manual+'#page=66'}>ZEISS Rev. 5 Fig. 15 (p. 66)</a> establishes component positions; <a href={brochure+'#page=37'}>ZEISS product info, table options</a> supplies the 1200 × 900 × 860 mm active-table dimensions. The <a href="https://www.ntu.edu.sg/images/librariesprovider12/specialized-facilities/microscopy-library/zeiss-lsm980.jpg?sfvrsn=2330d79e_1">NTU installed instrument photograph</a> visually corroborates the left scan module and the inverted eyepiece/stage silhouette. Its extra enclosure is not reconstructed. Individual housing and controls are visually inferred, not measured; the display desk is generic.</p>
<div class="grid"><figure><img width="660" height="440" src={base+'front.webp'} loading="lazy" alt="Original whole setup render with large table, module and generic display desk"/><figcaption>Original system render, not a photograph. Compared with ZEISS Fig. 15 for relative instrument positions.</figcaption></figure><figure><img width="660" height="440" src={base+'detail.webp'} loading="lazy" alt="Original front detail showing the left scan head, inverted stand and separate housings"/><figcaption>Original close-up compared with the NTU setup. The model consists of disconnected exterior shells and passive geometry.</figcaption></figure></div>
<div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Reference</th><th>Actual / interpretation</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Large active table</td><td>1200 × 900 × 860 mm</td><td>Metric reconstruction anchor. Not a measured stand or manufacturing drawing.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Synthetic sampling XYZ</td><td>0.10 × 0.12 × 0.20 µm spacing</td><td>Registered sample centers, 41 × 37 × 31 grid. Not a real imaging setup.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Independent spot FWHM</td><td>X 0.470964; Y 0.565157; Z 0.941928 µm</td><td>Numerically interpolated through the 3D center, within 0.016/0.019/0.030 µm sampling tolerances. See actual values in verification.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Background track</td><td>Relative constant 0.04</td><td>No FWHM; shared XYZ center aligns in all display planes.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Register held-out response</td><td>Measured bead-width comparison</td><td>No microscope acquisitions or held-out experimental validation. No resolution claim for ZEISS hardware or Airyscan processing.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p>The fictitious spot uses <code>I(x,y,z)=0.04+exp(−½Σ(coord/σ)²)</code> with authored σ values 0.20, 0.24, 0.40 µm. Plot planes use <code>coord = origin + index × spacing</code>. Width is measured across linearly interpolated half-amplitude crossings on each center line, not on the currently displayed slice. The exact independent reference is <code>2√(2 ln 2)σ</code>. Unresolved constant background returns null. The export includes the current sampled plane with axis order and units, plus metadata and center-line widths. No specimens, surface preparation, actual light source, biological data or hardware operation are included.</p>
<p><a href={base+'lsm980-static.glb'} download>Metric GLB</a> · <a href={base+'model.py'} download>Editable Blender generator</a> · <a href={base+'example-section.json'}>Output schema example</a> · <a href={base+'verification.json'}>Verification</a> · <a href={base+'xr-manifest.json'}>VR action contract</a>. No headset or live hardware was tested.</p></section>
</article></Layout>
<script>import '../../../../lib/equipment/12-03/browser.mjs';</script>
<style>
.lsm{max-width:76rem}.lsm .grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1.1rem}.lsm section{border-top:1px solid var(--border);padding:.8rem 0;margin:.8rem 0;min-width:0}.lsm .bar{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.44rem;margin:.55rem 0}.lsm .fields{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.48rem}.lsm label{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:.2rem;font-size:.92rem}.lsm input,.lsm select,.lsm button{font:inherit;color:var(--text);background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:.14rem;max-width:100%;min-width:0;min-height:2.4em;padding:.32em .52em}.lsm button{cursor:pointer}.lsm button:disabled{opacity:.52;cursor:default}.lsm .primary{color:white;background:#245350}.lsm #lsm-view{height:clamp(270px,31vw,435px);background:#d9dddf;touch-action:none}.lsm #lsm-view :global(canvas){width:100%;height:100%;display:block}.lsm #lsm-plot,.lsm img{width:100%;height:auto}.lsm #lsm-result{display:block;white-space:pre-line;margin:.45rem 0;font:1rem monospace}.lsm #lsm-status.error{color:#a54a34}.lsm .scroll{overflow:auto}.lsm table{border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.89rem}.lsm td,.lsm th{border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);text-align:left;padding:.45rem}.lsm figure{margin:.8rem 0}@media(max-width:800px){.lsm .grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
</style>
